The rendering core ports pbrt-v4's routines to Rust, following its source
operation for operation (PBR 4e, Pharr, Jakob and Humphreys). In particular,
these files are derived from it:

-   crates/umbra-spectrum/src/spectra/data.rs: the CIE 1931 colour-matching
    functions and the CIE D65 illuminant, from src/pbrt/util/spectrum.cpp.
-   crates/umbra-spectrum/build/cie_5nm.rs: the CIE 1931 colour-matching
    functions, the D65 illuminant and the sRGB matrices at 5 nm, from
    src/pbrt/cmd/rgb2spec_opt.cpp.
-   crates/umbra-spectrum/build/rgb2spec.rs: the RGB-to-spectrum optimiser of
    Jakob and Hanika, "A Low-Dimensional Function Space for Efficient Spectral
    Upsampling" (Computer Graphics Forum 38(2), 2019), from
    src/pbrt/cmd/rgb2spec_opt.cpp, and the table it generates at build time.
-   crates/umbra-spectrum/tests/umbra_spectrum/pbrt_v4/: tests ported from
    src/pbrt/util/spectrum_test.cpp and color_test.cpp, and a program that
    links pbrt-v4 to compute the values the tests compare with.

The Rust ports of pbrt-v4's routines in the other core crates
(umbra-math, umbra-sampling) and their tests under tests/*/pbrt_v4/ are
derived from pbrt-v4 likewise.
